GolangTAKServer is the native TAK service for the Pi 5 image.

It runs without Docker under OpenWrt procd and stores its configuration,
certificates, users, logs, and data under /opt/golangtakserver. During the
initial OpenMANET setup wizard, the password entered for the system root
account is also used for the GoLangTAKServer administrator account named
root. The password is passed through a temporary UCI value and removed after
the account update succeeds; the one-way password hash in /etc/shadow is not
read or copied. Complete the wizard with a non-empty password before using
the TAK dashboard.

The secure TAK listener is TLS 8089. The dashboard and enrollment endpoints use
HTTPS 8443 and 8446. For devices that cannot use the self-signed HTTPS/TLS
profile, the image also enables plain HTTP on 8088 and plain TAK TCP on 8087.
Those two listeners are unencrypted and must only be used on a trusted LAN or
MANET. The dashboard's iTAK section provides separate secure and plain-TCP QR
codes. Port 8080 remains reserved for the main OpenMANETd portal.

To change the GoLangTAK map, open the TAK dashboard, go to **Settings** →
**General**, and edit **Map tiles**. Use a tile URL containing `{z}`, `{x}`,
and `{y}`, for example
`https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png` when the node has Internet
access. For an offline MANET, use the URL of a tile server reachable from the
node. This changes the GoLangTAK map only; it does not change the OpenMANETd
portal on port 8080.

The packaged binary is GolangTAKServer 1.6.3 for Linux ARM64, built from the
upstream GoLangTAKServer source at commit
`57543215f44e90a65ae50c742f5b6580404409fd` with the OpenMANET plain-TCP QR
changes recorded in `package/golangtakserver/patches/100-plain-tcp-qr.patch`.
Its upstream license is installed at /opt/golangtakserver/LICENSE.
